# Dispatch kernel

**Invariant:** `lean_context ⇒ dispatch(heavy read | author | implement) off-seat; lead orchestrates`.
**Tier A** (`conductor`): ≤2 targeted reads to packetize; 0 in-seat edits, ssh/host ops, pytest; hop ≤35–40 turns or 2–3 milestones. **Tier B** (investigate/confer/sketch/review): scoped recon when ≥3 unknown loci; 0 implement writes or service mutations; split the remainder via `nest_under` or parent return. **Tier C** leaf homes omit this rule.

## Read side — `team_dispatch` over `Task`

`loci_unknown ∨ ≥3_files ∨ 2nd_speculative_grep ⇒ team_dispatch(op="generate", seat="cursor-sdk", lane="B")` — ¬ Cursor `Task` subagents (`team_dispatch` expands the pool).
`sparse(work_item) ⇒ recon ≺ implement` (`require_implement_ready` guards implement, ¬ conductor). Exempt: `mechanical`/`trivial`, or a dense spec with `files_expected` + AC. Bugfix on pattern P ⇒ sweep (`[quality:bug-class-sweep]`).

## Ladder + binder order

Mechanical implement: `lane="B"` `contract=implement` `model=cursor/composer-2.5` (omit `model=` ⇒ `cursor/grok-4.7`); throwaway worktree per top-level generate; `lane="A"` only on scope refusal or explicit shared-master request. Autonomous.
Investigate `cursor/grok-4.7` xhigh; conductor `cursor/grok-4.7` high; `OPEN FORK:` only. Autonomous.
Independent check: **ACTIVE** width · **`cdp/opus-5.5`** — announce `CDP: <trigger> — <why>`, proceed.
Live checkout: `cursor/grok-4.7` `contract=freeform` on cursor-sdk.
Binder: `cdp/opus-5.5` → `cdp/opus-5` → **`cdp/fable-5.1`** → `cdp/fable-5` (no bare `cdp/fable` unless Kaywan asks). `seat_unsure ⇒ consult(independent_binder)`; `binder_unsure ⇒ human`. CDP fail ⇒ no wait/retry; `cdp_fail_route`: `nested-grok` or `operator` (worker + `parent_thread` → web-anthropic). ¬ Cowork Ask.
