## Hard walls

- `anthropic/*` API admitted when credit-healthy.
- Non-primary `cursor/*` bind ⇒ **operator-gated** unless a standing rule/skill names the default.
- `judgment_closed ∧ mechanical_remainder ⇒ split`: bind (`none`) → nested `cursor-sdk` implement (`nest_under` lease holder).
- Before **any** `team_dispatch`: consult-routing gate; `busy_status` shows `agent_bus` + `stargate` + `git_integration_worker` up.
- Same input failed twice ⇒ no more retries of that input; one attempt of a different kind (replace the input) is allowed before REPEATED_FAILURE; a third retry of the same input is forbidden.
- `operator_names(param) ∧ ¬admits(param) ⇒ report(failure) ∧ wait`.

## Runbook binding

`cite(runbook:<id>) ⇒ load(section*) ∧ execute(seat-bound_steps)` before turn end. Partial cite ⇒ that section only. Skills/rules say *when*; the runbook owns *how*. Cite-from-memory = arm-without-relay.

## Front door

```
∀ operator_request:
  explicit override (/path-sim · /layer · root id · belt) ≺ tree
  mutates_durable_state ⇒ conductor session, bound to exactly one todo: work item
  else (answer · review · judgment, attended) ⇒ in-seat, threadless — reasoning-posture
    aperture; threadless ⇒ ¬mint work lane (`/orchestrate` births role:root; `checkpoint` = lean fire)
```

B legs spawn T0 conductor; the materializer refuses a non-todo `source_ref`. CHECKPOINT = reconstitution index only. `seat=cursor-sdk` closeout is silent SOP; operator-only ⇒ `status:needs-attended` + one recommended answer. Mutating Task prompts ⇒ inject kernel (`task-subagent-parity_ulg`). Native IDE Task ⇒ `/reasoning-posture` + Use-line unless closed procedure.
